<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Lambert of Hersfeld</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1028 – c. 1082</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Lambert of Hersfeld was a Benedictine monk of Hersfeld Abbey in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hesse">Hesse</a> and one of the leading German chroniclers of the 11th century. His Annals, a world chronicle that becomes detailed from 1040, give a vivid and hostile account of King Henry IV's reign, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saxons">Saxon</a> revolt and the Investiture Controversy up to 1077. He later became abbot of Hasungen.</p></div>
